---
import Entry from './Entry.astro';
import Dot from './Dot.astro';

// The rules every sketch follows.
const rules = [
  'Append only. A correction is a new sketch that says what it corrects.',
  'The clock stamps every entry. The agent never types a time.',
  'Never a secret. Key names and vault item names only.',
  'The person chooses at setup what else may go in: work only (the default), or everything.',
  'The person\'s words go in quotes, exactly as said.',
  'A guess is written as a guess.',
  'Never read whole. The open items, the newest In flight block, the newest work list, the last 150 lines. The rest by grep.',
];
---

<Entry id="sketchbook" label="07 · The sketchbook" title="What is happening right now.">
  <p class="standfirst prose">The sketchbook is the agent's running notes. Each entry is a sketch.</p>

  <div class="spread">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The portrait says who the agent is. A landscape says what is true
        in one area of work. Neither says what happened this morning, what
        is running, or what waits on the person. After a compaction, the
        portrait gives the agent back its character. The sketchbook lets it
        pick the thread back up.
      </p>
      <p>
        A sketch is one line, stamped by the clock with a small command,
        <code>note</code>. Two kinds of block sit among the sketches: the In
        flight block (waiting on the person, running, just finished) and the
        work list. The newest block of each kind wins. Nothing is ever
        edited in place.
      </p>
      <p>
        A painter keeps a sketchbook every day, and most of it is never
        shown. What keeps coming back gets painted properly. A pattern that
        shows up in the sketches again and again becomes a rule in the
        portrait, a fact in a landscape, or a stroke.
      </p>
      <p>
        One file per month. A pointer, <code>current.md</code>, always names
        the current month, so nothing that reads the sketchbook needs to
        know about months. On the first night of a month a small script
        starts the new file with an open items page: the newest In flight
        block, the newest work list and the open lists, carried over. The
        old month stays as it was, searchable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="margin">
      <figure class="diagram route-figure">
        <ul class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <li><Dot kind="none" />the sketchbook folder</li>
        </ul>
        <ol class="route route-open" aria-label="A month change, in order">
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>a timer, just after midnight</b>
            <span>did the month change? if not, nothing happens</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>the script takes the lock</b>
            <span>a note waits a moment</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>the new month</b>
            <span>open items carried, re-stamped, marked carried</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>current.md moves</b>
            <span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span> the old month is never changed</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </figure>

      <!-- A made-up page in the exact format. -->
      <figure class="diagram studio-page">
        <figcaption class="leaf-cap">sketchbook/2027-02.md, an invented day</figcaption>
        <pre class="md">- 2027-02-03 15:10 CET Lesson on Friday.
- 2027-02-03 15:12 CET IN FLIGHT (current):
  W. Oven repair: confirm Thursday
  R. 14:50 Pattern cards: printing
  F. 15:05 Allergen note sent</pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="security">
    <div>
      <h3>The rules</h3>
      <ul class="limits">
        {rules.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>Where it sits</h3>
      <ul class="limits">
        <li>The session-start hook names the parts to read and the scope.</li>
        <li>The nudge hook asks for the sketchbook to be brought up to date, and warns past 400 KB in one month.</li>
        <li>A landscape holds no history. The sketchbook keeps it.</li>
        <li>The studio's journal is the agent's own. The sketchbook is the work.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="aside-note">
        The sketchbook is the sixth part of Essence: two small commands in
        <code>scripts/</code>, <code>note</code> and
        <code>sketchbook-rotate</code>, and a folder of month files.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Entry>
